com/","observedAt":"2026-09-17T04:25:52.790Z","title":"Equine Bodywork Online","excerpt":"0 Skip to Content Login Account Member Access Open Menu Close Menu Login Account Member Access Open Menu Close Menu Login Account Member Access The essential bodywork program for every horse. Follow along with licensed Equine Massage Therapist Kara O'Laughlin while she walks you through, step-by-step, the foundational massage techniques to prehab your own horse. PRE•HABpriː.hæb (Noun)Short for prehabilitation, prehab is the practice of enhancing muscle and joint function in order to reduce risk of injury, increase physical performance, and help maintain unrestricted mobility. How EBO Works: 1 — Select CategoryEnhancing Performance or Relieving Tension 2 — Watch & LearnVideos with unique routines for each muscle 3 — Get Hands OnFollow along with innovative Audio Guides ✔ Innovative Hands On Videos & Audio Guides✔ Filtering system to target specific muscles✔ Access to members only online community✔ No subscription SALE $229 (reg. $329) ✔ 25 exercises with more on the way✔ Filtering system to target specific muscles✔ Access to members only online community✔ No subscription SALE $160 (reg. $229) ✔ All EBO + GPW perks included✔ Save 35% with this combo✔ Access to members only online community✔ No subscription SALE $324 (reg. $499) Relieve Tension From canter leads to hoojack issues, learn how to help your equine partner through some of the toughest training problems by releasing tension and developing correct muscle memory. Our videos, and our audio guides, take you through each step to release tension in muscle groups that are individually specified for the most common problems our horses face. What's inside Relieve Tension: Scroll Left or Right Enhance Performance Increase your horse’s range of motion, flexibility, stability, and release tension in the crucial muscles they need to perform at their peak. We’ve narrowed down the most common performance enhancement requests from the field and have categorized each one so you can pick and choose a plan that works for you and your horse’s needs at any given moment in their riding career. What's inside Enhance Performance: Scroll Left or Right Audio Guides With the guidance of a professional equine therapist taking you through each and every step, you will effectively and easily relieve tension and ensure your horse is performing at its best. From pressure to stroke speed, the audio guides are designed for you to lis\n公开联系片段：\n页面原文: @EquineBodyworkOnlineTeam@EquineBodyworkOnline.com\nHTML href: mailto:Team@EquineBodyworkOnline.com","contentHash":"5d10da257e9d466c7e34745bd80eea46150a8f92e573f9d6317e4a43638f7570","contentType":"text/html;charset=utf-8","depth":0,"sourceKind":"website","retrievals":[{"requestedUrl":"https://equinebodyworkonline.com/","observedAt":"2026-09-17T04:25:52.790Z"},{"requestedUrl":"https://www.equinebodyworkonline.com/","observedAt":"2026-09-17T04:25:58.894Z"}]},{"id":"web:e32890f0869a6e030be4d29c","requestedUrl":"https://www.equinebodyworkonline.com/about","finalUrl":"https://www.equinebodyworkonline.com/about","observedAt":"2026-09-17T04:25:57.939Z","title":"About — Equine Bodywork Online","excerpt":"0 Skip to Content Login Account Member Access Open Menu Close Menu Login Account Member Access Open Menu Close Menu Login Account Member Access Meet the people behind EBO. Brice and Kara have combined their unique skills and experience to bring something truly revolutionary to the equestrian world. Kara’s knowledge and passion for equine anatomy & movement, together with Brice’s commercial filmmaking experience make EBO both innovated and inspirational. Kara O’Laughlin, L.A.M.PInstructor & Co-Founder Kara is a nationally recognized equine sports massage therapist and bodyworker based in the Pacific Northwest of the United States. A graduate of Northwest School of Animal Massage, and licensed through the Washington State Department of Health as a Large Animal Massage Practitioner, her work focuses on performance enhancement and tension release techniques for the equine athlete and pleasure horse. Through massage, range of motion stretches, acupressure, and other manual manipulation modalities, Kara has helped thousands of horses feel their best and perform at the top of their sport, including Grand Prix dressage horses, 5 star event horses, World Champion Reining horses, and FEI jumpers. She is passionate about ensuring every horse is able to perform comfortably, whether it be in the upper levels or simply heading out on the trail. Prior to her career as an equine sports therapist, Kara worked in international higher education. She loves to blend her passion for equine bodywork, her love for anatomy, and her skills as an educator to bring knowledge and awareness to horse owners. She believes every horse and rider can benefit from equine bodywork and is thrilled to offer Equine Bodywork Online so horse lovers can reap the profound benefits of working on their own horses. Brice Van BarenContent Creator & Co-Founder The man behind the camera who makes the magic happen — Brice has been creating digital art for over 20 years and brings a cinematic perspective to his creative work. Brice blends his Video/Photo/Design talents to bring a unique perspective to the content that he creates. As a private pilot himself, Brice is also the founder of the largest social aviation network for North American pilots. To date, Flights Above holds 24,000+ Members and is a key platform for anyone involved in the aviation industry. When he is not creating content for Equine Bodywork\n公开联系片段：\n页面原文: @EquineBodyworkOnlineTeam@EquineBodyworkOnline.com\nHTML href: mailto:Team@EquineBodyworkOnline.com","contentHash":"9ed96802a8ade0036c45f896748837f4937c3214f13be240c499f98702e0068a","contentType":"text/html;charset=utf-8","depth":1,"sourceKind":"website","retrievals":[{"requestedUrl":"https://www.equinebodyworkonline.com/about","observedAt":"2026-09-17T04:25:57.939Z"}